cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "PatentPincer: an autonomous patentability analyst over SerpApi prior art"
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Sarkar"
    given-names: "Dipankar"
repository-code: "https://github.com/doom2quake/patentpincer"
abstract: >-
  Describe an invention in one sentence and PatentPincer searches the prior art,
  fetches the numbered claims of the closest references, compares the invention
  element by element, and returns a decision-ready verdict (CLEAR, NEEDS_REVIEW,
  HIGH_OVERLAP, or SEARCH_UNAVAILABLE) with citations. SerpApi's Google Patents,
  Patents Details and Scholar engines are the load-bearing data backbone; the
  analyst is a skill graph built on the doom2quake agent-core, with SerpApi spend
  held behind a rate guardrail and the verdict routed to the right destination. A
  search that did not succeed, an empty reference set, or claim text that was
  never retrieved all fail closed, and never to a clearance.
keywords:
  - prior-art-search
  - patentability
  - serpapi
  - google-patents
  - autonomous-agent
license: MIT
version: "0.1.0"
date-released: "2026-08-19"
